# Installation
I'm following the quickstart guide on SIDERO's website and currently this is for Talos Linux, version 1.14. I'll worry about bare-metal install on Rasperbby pie 5 later - today, its just about getting this OS up and running to see it in action. 

This guide walks us through starting a local Talos Linux cluster using Docker and talosctl in a few minutes. Because I'm on a MAC I will follow this install guide from Talos [website](https://docs.siderolabs.com/talos/v1.14/getting-started/quickstart), but based on the doc's it appears you could do this the documentation already seems a bit odd, because the first section says:

> A short guide on setting up... Talos Linux cluster locally with Docker.

And then continues with the pre-req's being:
- talosctl: On macOS or Linux, install talosctl by running the command below. For other systems, see the "talosctl documentation":
  - brew tap siderolabs/tap
  - brew trust siderolabs/tap
  - brew install siderolabs/tap/talosctl
- kubectl

And while kubectl is straight forward and I would expect us to know how to install this. The pre-req's, don't say nothing about docker install. But yes, assuming we are interested in talos, I'll make the assumtion we know how docker works, and forgive the poor doc's team at Talos... 

Also, luckly for me I'm using MAC, so `brew` install, for the `talosctl`, will work, but, if your not on MAC.... 
If I were Talos, instead of making us jump around for it, I personally would call out on this quickstart page, the `curl` command for other OS's should work too, as I found in this section on [this page](https://docs.siderolabs.com/talos/v1.14/getting-started/talosctl#alternative-install). Basically you can `curl` install `talosctl` for the following OS's (for both amd64 and arm64):
- macOS
- Linux
- WSL on Windows
> curl -sL https://talos.dev/install | sh

