Now to generate the cluster, the quickstart say's just this one command:
`talosctl cluster create docker`
On first glance, I though "docker" was the name of the cluster, but after checking the cli [docs](https://docs.siderolabs.com/talos/v1.14/reference/cli#talosctl-cluster-create-docker), the keyword "docker" is actually providing talosctl the argument for a `docker cluster`... I guess there is also a "create dev" and "create qemu", but I won't bother getting into that now... 
To name the cluster, like i did, just pass the flag `--name`.
> `talosctl cluster create docker --name devTalosCluster`
I also noted the command `talosctl cluster destroy` if something went wrong durring creation.
